    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f65554b1_09098297",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T10:48:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "get_shadow_vcpu() is only called by __pkvm_vcpu_load(). Would it make sense to rename it to load_shadow_vcpu()?",
      "parentUuid": "ad915c51_16d85802",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "521e2f1780da7543d07183f86ada76de57e79567",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8900dada_15ba1b57",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1729538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T11:01:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe.\n\nI think what I dislike is that there are two notions of \u0027loaded\u0027:\n- the vcpu loaded attribute\n- the per-CPU pointer\n\nIdeally, we\u0027d drop the attribute altogether, and replace it with a pointer to the per-CPU pointer indicating *where* it is loaded. This xchg() becomes a cmpxchg() expecting NULL as the previous value, and the function can populate the per-CPU pointer with the vcpu pointer.\n\nThis rids us of some code in __pkvm_vcpu_load(), and the function now deserves its load_shadow_vcpu() name.",
      "parentUuid": "f65554b1_09098297",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "521e2f1780da7543d07183f86ada76de57e79567",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3915b42d_667931b2",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T11:06:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good. Will do that as a patch to follow this one (in this series).",
      "parentUuid": "8900dada_15ba1b57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "521e2f1780da7543d07183f86ada76de57e79567",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08420543_87b6887b",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T13:18:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I got confused myself a bit with the purpose of this. Let me just recap and backtrack a bit.\n\nThe cleanup for the __pkvm_vcpu_load() has been done in a future patch, but Will suggested to hold on to that until later, since it\u0027s not a bugfix.\n\nAs for this boolean, its purpose is to ensure that the shadow vcpu isn\u0027t loaded on more than one (real/physical) cpu. So I don\u0027t think I can achieve the same effect by replacing it with the per-cpu pointer.",
      "parentUuid": "3915b42d_667931b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "521e2f1780da7543d07183f86ada76de57e79567",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffd39103_69376c00",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1729538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T14:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All I am saying is that you can replace the boolean with the address of the per-CPU pointer holding the address of the vcpu. If it is NULL, the vcpu isn\u0027t loaded. Conversely, if it is !NULL, it is loaded.\n\nPassing the address of the per-CPU pointer to this function *and* having it to update the per-CPU state as well makes it self-contained: if this function return success, the vcpu is flagged as loaded (it contains a !NULL pointer), the per-CPU state is up-to-date, and we can even deduce which CPU the vcpu is loaded on by looking at the stored pointer, which is invaluable for debugging.\n\nNone of that needs to happen right now, but it would be a good cleanup.",
      "parentUuid": "08420543_87b6887b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "521e2f1780da7543d07183f86ada76de57e79567",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
